<title>ITALY: Olivetti resumes trade at 465 lire, down 9.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Olivetti resumes trade at 465 lire, down 9.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in crisis-hit Olivetti resumed trading after their latest suspension at 465 lire, down 9.9 percent, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The stock was first suspended limit down about 20 minutes into the morning stock market session when it plunged to 465 lire after opening at 498 lire against a Monday close at 516.5.</p>
<p>At 1222 GMT it was quoted at 467 lire, down 9.58 percent, in volume of over 31 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
